---
// ============================================================================
// Understanding Binary Search Guide (Route: /guides/binary-search/)
// ============================================================================

import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Understanding Binary Search & O(log n) Efficiency"
  description="A deep dive into divide-and-conquer searching, pointer tracking (Low, Mid, High), integer overflow prevention, and logarithmic complexity."
  currentRoute="/guides/binary-search/"
>
  <div class="guide-article-container container">
    <nav class="breadcrumb-nav" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <ol class="breadcrumb-list">
        <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
        <li class="separator" aria-hidden="true">/</li>
        <li><a href="/guides/">Guides</a></li>
        <li class="separator" aria-hidden="true">/</li>
        <li aria-current="page">Binary Search</li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <header class="article-header">
      <div class="badge-row">
        <span class="category-badge">SEARCH ALGORITHMS</span>
        <span class="badge-pill">O(log n) COMPLEXITY</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="article-title">Understanding Binary Search & O(log n) Efficiency</h1>
      <p class="article-lead">
        Learn how Binary Search divides sorted arrays in half with each comparison, finding elements in billions of records in under 32 operations.
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Interactive Callout -->
    <div class="interactive-callout">
      <div class="callout-icon" aria-hidden="true">&gt;_</div>
      <div class="callout-content">
        <h2 class="callout-title">Interactive Tool Available</h2>
        <p class="callout-desc">Step through pointers, array dimming, and synchronized code line-by-line.</p>
      </div>
      <a href="/visualizers/binary-search/" class="btn-callout">Launch Visualizer →</a>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 1: The Core Mechanism -->
    <section class="guide-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">1. The Divide-and-Conquer Principle</h2>
      <p class="guide-text">
        In linear search, an algorithm examines every item sequentially from index 0 to $n - 1$, taking up to $n$ comparisons in the worst case. 
        If the data is sorted, we can do dramatically better by inspecting the <strong>middle element</strong>:
      </p>

      <ul class="guide-bullets">
        <li>If <code>array[mid] == target</code>: The target is found; terminate immediately.</li>
        <li>If <code>array[mid] &lt; target</code>: Because the array is sorted, the target cannot exist in the left half. Discard indices $[0 \dots mid]$ and search $[mid + 1 \dots high]$.</li>
        <li>If <code>array[mid] &gt; target</code>: The target cannot exist in the right half. Discard indices $[mid \dots high]$ and search $[low \dots mid - 1]$.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 2: Integer Overflow -->
    <section class="guide-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">2. Why We Calculate Mid as low + floor((high - low) / 2)</h2>
      <p class="guide-text">
        Many textbooks write the midpoint calculation as <code>(low + high) / 2</code>. While algebraically equivalent, in systems with 32-bit signed integers, 
        adding <code>low + high</code> will overflow to negative numbers when their sum exceeds $2^{31} - 1 = 2,147,483,647$.
      </p>

      <div class="code-comparison-box">
        <div class="code-col bad">
          <span class="code-col-label">Naive (Overflow Bug):</span>
          <code>const mid = Math.floor((low + high) / 2);</code>
        </div>
        <div class="code-col good">
          <span class="code-col-label">Robust (Overflow Safe):</span>
          <code>const mid = low + Math.floor((high - low) / 2);</code>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 3: The 3 Most Common Pitfalls -->
    <section class="guide-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">3. The Three Most Common Beginner Bugs</h2>
      <div class="pitfalls-grid">
        <div class="pitfall-card">
          <h3 class="pitfall-title">1. Loop Condition: low &lt; high vs. low &le; high</h3>
          <p class="pitfall-desc">
            Using <code>while (low &lt; high)</code> fails when the search narrows to a single-element range where <code>low == high</code>. Always use <code>while (low &le; high)</code> unless writing an exclusive upper-bound bisect.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="pitfall-card">
          <h3 class="pitfall-title">2. Forgetting to Shift Past Mid (mid &plusmn; 1)</h3>
          <p class="pitfall-desc">
            Writing <code>low = mid</code> or <code>high = mid</code> instead of <code>mid + 1</code> / <code>mid - 1</code> causes an infinite loop when <code>high - low == 1</code>, because <code>mid</code> evaluates to <code>low</code> repeatedly.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="pitfall-card">
          <h3 class="pitfall-title">3. Running on Unsorted Arrays</h3>
          <p class="pitfall-desc">
            If the array is unsorted, the elimination assumption is false and binary search will return incorrect "not found" results. Sorting first takes $O(n \log n)$, which is only worthwhile if searching multiple times.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Complexity Summary Table -->
    <section class="guide-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">Complexity Summary</h2>
      <div class="table-scroll-wrapper">
        <table class="data-table" aria-label="Binary Search Complexity">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Case</th>
              <th scope="col">Comparisons</th>
              <th scope="col">Explanation</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Best Case</strong></td>
              <td><code>O(1)</code></td>
              <td>Target is located directly at the initial midpoint.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Average Case</strong></td>
              <td><code>O(log n)</code></td>
              <td>Interval halves each step; on $n = 1,000,000$, $\approx 20$ comparisons.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Worst Case</strong></td>
              <td><code>O(log n)</code></td>
              <td>Target is at boundaries or absent; interval reduced to 0 elements.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Space Complexity</strong></td>
              <td><code>O(1)</code></td>
              <td>Iterative algorithm uses only 3 pointer variables in memory.</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <footer class="article-footer">
      <div class="footer-nav-row">
        <a href="/guides/big-o-cheat-sheet/" class="footer-link-back">← Big-O Cheat Sheet</a>
        <a href="/guides/sorting-algorithms/" class="footer-link-next">Next Guide: Comparison Sorting Demystified →</a>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .guide-article-container {
    padding-top: var(--space-8);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-16);
    max-width: var(--reading-max);
  }

  .breadcrumb-nav { margin-bottom: var(--space-6); }
  .breadcrumb-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    list-style: none;
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
  .breadcrumb-list a { color: var(--color-text-secondary); transition: color var(--transition-fast); }
  .breadcrumb-list a:hover { color: var(--color-primary-400); }
  .separator { color: var(--color-border); }

  .article-header { margin-bottom: var(--space-8); }
  .badge-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }
  .category-badge {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-primary-400);
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }
  .badge-pill {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-cyan-400);
    background-color: rgba(6, 182, 212, 0.1);
    border: 1px solid rgba(6, 182, 212, 0.25);
    padding: 2px 8px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  }

  .article-title {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    line-height: var(--leading-tight);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-tight);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }
  .article-lead {
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
  }

  /* Interactive Callout */
  .interactive-callout {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(6, 182, 212, 0.1) 0%, rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.1) 100%);
    border: 1px solid rgba(6, 182, 212, 0.3);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: var(--space-5);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-10);
  }
  .callout-icon { font-size: 2rem; }
  .callout-content { flex: 1; min-width: 200px; }
  .callout-title {
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    margin-bottom: 2px;
  }
  .callout-desc {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }
  .btn-callout {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-primary-text);
    background-color: var(--color-primary-600);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-primary-500);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: 10px 16px;
    min-height: 40px;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    transition: all var(--transition-fast);
  }
  .btn-callout:hover {
    background-color: var(--color-primary-500);
    transform: translateY(-1px);
  }

  .guide-section { margin-bottom: var(--space-10); }
  .section-title {
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-2);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle);
  }
  .guide-text {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }
  .guide-bullets {
    list-style: disc;
    padding-left: var(--space-6);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
  }

  /* Code Comparison */
  .code-comparison-box {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }
  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .code-comparison-box { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
  }
  .code-col {
    background-color: var(--color-bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: var(--space-4);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }
  .code-col.bad { border-color: rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.3); }
  .code-col.good { border-color: rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.3); }
  .code-col-label { font-size: var(--text-xs); font-weight: 700; }
  .code-col.bad .code-col-label { color: #f87171; }
  .code-col.good .code-col-label { color: var(--color-emerald-400); }
  .code-col code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    background-color: var(--color-slate-950);
    padding: var(--space-2);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
  }

  /* Pitfalls Grid */
  .pitfalls-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }
  .pitfall-card {
    background-color: var(--color-bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: var(--space-5);
  }
  .pitfall-title {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-amber-400);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }
  .pitfall-desc {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
  }

  .table-scroll-wrapper { overflow-x: auto; }
  .data-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    text-align: left;
  }
  .data-table th {
    background-color: var(--color-bg-elevated);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .data-table td {
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
  }
  .data-table code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--color-cyan-400);
    background-color: rgba(6, 182, 212, 0.1);
    padding: 1px 4px;
    border-radius: 3px;
  }

  .article-footer {
    padding-top: var(--space-6);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }
  .footer-nav-row {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .footer-link-back { color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .footer-link-back:hover { color: var(--color-primary-400); }
  .footer-link-next { color: var(--color-primary-400); }
  .footer-link-next:hover { color: #ffffff; }
</style>
